{
    "file": "Competitive_Strategies_and_Value_Innovation.docx",
    "title": "Competitive Strategies and Value Innovation",
    "duration": "3 Days",
    "overview": [
        "Sustainable competitive advantage requires organizations to understand where competition is heading, make deliberate strategic choices, and create value in ways that are difficult to imitate. Competing only on existing industry factors can lead to price pressure, incremental improvement, and strategic similarity. Value innovation challenges organizations to rethink what customers and stakeholders value and to redesign the combination of benefits, costs, experiences, and capabilities that define their competitive position.",
        "This three-day course provides managers and strategy professionals with practical frameworks for analyzing competitive environments, understanding sources of advantage, identifying strategic gaps, evaluating competitors, segmenting value, and creating differentiated strategic positions. Participants will also explore value innovation principles, strategic canvases, the eliminate-reduce-raise-create framework, noncustomer analysis, business-model choices, and the translation of strategic ideas into executable initiatives.",
        "Through competitive-analysis exercises, case studies, strategic mapping, value-curve development, option evaluation, and implementation planning, participants will learn to move from market understanding to clear strategic choices that create distinctive and defensible value."
    ],
    "audience": [
        "Senior managers, department heads, strategy and planning professionals, business-development managers, marketing managers, product and service leaders, innovation managers, transformation professionals, business-unit leaders, and managers involved in competitive positioning, growth, strategic planning, or value creation."
    ],
    "methodology": [
        "The course uses an applied methodology combining short presentations, competitive-strategy cases, industry and competitor analysis, strategic-group mapping, customer-value analysis, strategy-canvas exercises, value-curve development, eliminate-reduce-raise-create workshops, noncustomer analysis, strategic-option evaluation, group discussion, and implementation planning. Participants apply the tools to realistic organizational and market situations."
    ],
    "competencies": [
        "Competitive analysis",
        "Strategic positioning",
        "Customer and stakeholder value analysis",
        "Value innovation",
        "Strategic differentiation",
        "Competitive intelligence",
        "Strategic option development",
        "Business-model thinking",
        "Strategic decision making",
        "Market opportunity identification",
        "Strategic prioritization",
        "Strategy implementation"
    ],
    "objectivesIntro": [
        "By the end of the course, participants will be able to:"
    ],
    "objectives": [
        "Analyze the competitive forces and structural characteristics of an industry or sector.",
        "Identify current and emerging competitors, substitutes, and alternative sources of value.",
        "Assess organizational sources of competitive advantage and strategic vulnerability.",
        "Evaluate different approaches to competitive positioning and differentiation.",
        "Map the factors on which organizations currently compete.",
        "Apply value innovation principles to challenge established competitive assumptions.",
        "Use the strategy canvas and value curve to compare strategic profiles.",
        "Apply the eliminate-reduce-raise-create framework to redesign customer or stakeholder value.",
        "Explore noncustomers and unmet needs as sources of strategic opportunity.",
        "Evaluate strategic options based on value, differentiation, feasibility, risk, and sustainability.",
        "Translate competitive and value-innovation choices into focused implementation priorities."
    ],
